<?import javafx.scene.control.ScrollPane?>
<?import javafx.scene.layout.VBox?>
<?import javafx.scene.text.Text?>
<?import javafx.scene.text.TextFlow?>
<?import javafx.scene.image.ImageView?>
<?import javafx.scene.layout.HBox?>
<?import javafx.scene.control.Label?>

<!-- The whole scene is scrollable -->
<ScrollPane
        xmlns="http://javafx.com/javafx/21"
        xmlns:fx="http://javafx.com/fxml/1"
        fx:controller="com.example.game.gui.HowToPlayController"
        styleClass="blackBackground"
        stylesheets="styles.css"
        fitToWidth="true"
>
   <!-- Everything is stacked vertically -->
   <VBox styleClass="howToPlayContainer">
      <TextFlow>
         <!-- Simple heading of the section -->
         <Text styleClass="howToPlayHeading">Game Manual</Text>
      </TextFlow>

      <TextFlow styleClass="textJustify">
         <Text styleClass="whiteText">
            Welcome to the built-in manual of game Light Bulbs. Here you can find all necessary
            information about the game, how to play it aw well as information about some hidden features.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <!-- Chapter with its text -->
      <TextFlow>
         <Text styleClass="howToPlayChapter">Basic Principles</Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <TextFlow styleClass="textJustify">
         <Text styleClass="whiteText">
            The game is about rotating power source, light bulb and wire cells until all
            light bulbs are powered on. So the main goal is to connect all light bulbs to the power source.
            You can either load your save and continue playing it or generate a new game.
            Difficulty can be modified by setting the size of a game map, changing timer duration,
            changing count of empty cells and setting shuffling strength.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>

      <TextFlow>
         <Text styleClass="howToPlayChapter">Cell Types</Text>
      </TextFlow>

      <!-- H-Boxes with an image and descriptor -->

      <HBox spacing="10" alignment="CENTER_LEFT">
         <ImageView fx:id="powerSourceImage" fitHeight="50.0" fitWidth="50.0" />
         <Label styleClass="whiteLabel" text="Power Source" />
      </HBox>

      <HBox spacing="10" alignment="CENTER_LEFT">
         <ImageView fx:id="lightBulbImage" fitHeight="50.0" fitWidth="50.0" />
         <Label styleClass="whiteLabel" text="Light Bulb" />
      </HBox>

      <HBox spacing="10" alignment="CENTER_LEFT">
         <ImageView fx:id="wireImage" fitHeight="50.0" fitWidth="50.0" />
         <Label styleClass="whiteLabel" text="Wire" />
      </HBox>
      <!-- Chapter with its text -->
      <TextFlow styleClass="textJustify">
         <Text styleClass="whiteText">
            These cell types come in different configurations. The configurations denote which of their
            sides can be connected and whether they are powered or not. Power source is always powered on.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <!-- Chapter with its text -->
      <TextFlow>
         <Text styleClass="howToPlayChapter">Basic Controls</Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <TextFlow styleClass="textJustify">
         <Text styleClass="whiteText">
            The game is controlled by clicking on the game cells, which rotates them by 90 degrees. Empty cells
            cannot be rotated. You win the game when all light bulbs are powered. If you fail to light them before the timer
            ends, then you lose the game. After the game is finished (won or lost), the game cells become inactive to your clicks.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <!-- Chapter with its text -->
      <TextFlow>
         <Text styleClass="howToPlayChapter">Help View</Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <TextFlow styleClass="textJustify">
         <Text styleClass="whiteText">
            Help View shows you how many rotations each game cell needs to be in the right position.
            It can be opened by pressing its button in the game menu. Finishing the game automatically
            closes the Help View window. Do not use it too much. That would be cheating!!
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <!-- Chapter with its text -->
      <TextFlow>
         <Text styleClass="howToPlayChapter">Undo and Redo</Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <TextFlow styleClass="textJustify">
         <Text styleClass="whiteText">
            The game allows you to undo and redo your clicks. To use this feature, you can press the buttons
            with the same names in the game menu. Undo of a turn does not decrease your turn count. This feature
            disables when the game finishes.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <!-- Chapter with its text -->
      <TextFlow>
         <Text styleClass="howToPlayChapter">Auto Solving</Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <TextFlow styleClass="textJustify">
         <Text styleClass="whiteText">
            If you feel tired, then you can use the built-in auto solver, which will lock the game
            and solve the game step by step. Once turned on, it cannot be disabled
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <!-- Chapter with its text -->
      <TextFlow>
         <Text styleClass="howToPlayChapter">Gameplay Tips</Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <TextFlow styleClass="textJustify">
         <Text styleClass="whiteText">
            Hovering over a cell shows tooltip with the count of total rotations so far. If you
            do that after the game finishes, information about the remaining count of turns is
            also displayed. State of unfinished game can be also saved and loaded later on.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>
   </VBox>
</ScrollPane>
